From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] soundwire: qcom: let the last data port be allocated

Data ports are numbered from 1 to nports: bit 0 of port_mask is reserved
and pconfig[1..nports] hold the per-port properties from the DT. Since
commit 6ccec91c3535 ("soundwire: qcom: Fix port exhaustion check in
stream_alloc_ports"), qcom_swrm_stream_alloc_ports() rejects any port
number >= nports, which takes the last port out of use as well: a slave
whose qcom,port-mapping names it fails hw_params with "All ports busy",
and the search for a free port never reaches it either.

On a Huawei MateBook E Go the right WSA8835's VI sense output is mapped
to port 8 of the speaker controller (6 dout and 2 din ports), so with VI
sense enabled no speaker stream could be started.

Bound the search and the check by nports + 1, which keeps the exhaustion
check that commit added.

Fixes: 6ccec91c3535 ("soundwire: qcom: Fix port exhaustion check in stream_alloc_ports")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/soundwire/qcom.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
index b288218f6..65b92069a 100644
--- a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
@@ -1259,7 +1259,8 @@ static int qcom_swrm_stream_alloc_ports(struct qcom_swrm_ctrl *ctrl,
 			continue;
 
 		port_mask = &ctrl->port_mask;
-		maxport = ctrl->nports;
+		/* Ports are numbered 1 to nports, bit 0 of port_mask is reserved */
+		maxport = ctrl->nports + 1;
 
 		list_for_each_entry(s_rt, &m_rt->slave_rt_list, m_rt_node) {
 			slave = s_rt->slave;
